  "raw_text": "243\n\nTakaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stop, to impede, to hinder, to delay, to conclude, to stay, to remain, to take a position, to dwell, to\nabide, to reside, to live\n \n/ detenerse, impedir, obstaculizar, retrasar, concluir, quedarse, permanecer, tomar una\nposición, habitar, acatar, residir, vivir\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nPearl Lagoon takaskisna\n \n–\n \nI live in Pearl Lagoon\n \n/ Yo vivo en Laguna de Perlas)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nli ba takaskras\n \nauhwan\n \n–\n \nit rained without stopping\n \n/ llovió sin parar)\n\nAlki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hold back, to keep back, to detain, to hinder, to control\n \n/ retener, contener, detener,\nobstaculizar, controlar\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb84\n):\n \nJisas pâsa bara lî alki takaskaia sip kan\n \n–\n \nJesus was able to control the wind and the rain\n \n/ Jesús pudo\ncontrolar el viento y la lluvia)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n \n(\nmwb-05/22\n):\n \nWan brinka nani alki takaskaia dukiara, Jehova ra bik takaia sa ai hilpka wankbia.\n \n–\n \nIn order to\ncontrol our desires, we must beg Jehovah to give us his help.\n \n/ Para controlar nuestros deseos, debemos suplicar a Jehová\nque nos dé su ayuda.)\n\nAi wîna alki takaskan lâka ba briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have self-control over their body, to have control over\nthemselves\n \n/ tener autocontrol sobre su cuerpo, tener control sobre sí mismos\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nJosep ba ai muihnika nani ra kaikan taim, ai wîna alki takaskan lâka ba brin.\n \n–\n \nWhen Joseph\nsaw his brothers, he had control over himself.\n \n/ Cuando José vio a sus hermanos, tenía control sobre sí mismo.)\n\nAlki takaskras\n \n(v-neg)\n \n–\n \nnot hold back, not keep back, not detain, not hinder, not control\n \n/ no retener, no\ncontener, no detener, no obstaculizar, no controlar\n\nKupia alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control (the) heart, to have self-control, to deal patiently with someone or\nsomething\n \n/ controlar (el) corazón, tener autocontrol, tratar pacientemente con alguien o algo\n\nKupia alki takaskan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nself-control, control of the heart, to have control of the heart\n \n/\nautocontrol, control del corazón, tener control del corazón, autodominio\n \n(See also/ Ver\ntambién:\n \nWîna alki takaskan l\nâ\nka\n)\n\nTwisi alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control the tongue\n \n/ controlar la lengua\n\nWîna alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control the body, to control oneself\n \n/ controlar el cuerpo, controlarse a uno\nmismo\n\nWan wîna alki takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto control our body, to control ourselves\n \n/ controlar nuestro cuerpo,\ncontrolarnos a nosotros mismos\n\nWîna alki takaskan lâka\n \n(a/t:\n \nWîna alki takaskaia lâka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ncontrol of the body, self-control\n \n/\ncontrol del cuerpo, autodominio\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nKupia alki takaskan lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/21\n):\n \nKristian nani sut ba rum diaia dukiara wîna alki takaskaia lâka ba praptis mauna nit\nsa\n \n–\n \nAll Christians need to exercise self-control with regards to drinking alcohol\n \n/ Todos los cristianos\ndeben ejercer el autocontrol con respecto al consumo de alcohol)\n\nIp takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto stop, to detain\n \n/ parar, detener\n\nSwirka takaskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to stop\n \n/ permitir parar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfg1\n):\n \nSwirka mai takasbiara\n \n–\n \nDon’t allow to stop you\n \n/ No permitas detenerte)\n\nTakas!\n \n(v-imp)\n \n–\n \nStop!, Stay!\n \n/ ¡Alto!, ¡Quédate!\n\nTakasbiara\n \n(v-alt-proh)\n \n–\n \nnot to stop\n/\nstay, do not stop\n/\nstay, we are not to stop\n/\nstay, one is not to stop\n/\nstay, we\nmust not stop\n/\nstay, one must not stop\n/stay / no parar/quedarse, no debemos parar/ quedarse, uno no debe\nparar/quedarse\n\nTakaskras\n \n(v-neg)\n \n–\n \nnot stop, not impede, not hinder, not delay, not conclude, not stay, not remain, not dwell, not\nreside\n \n/ no parar, no impedir, no obstaculizar, no retrasar, no concluir, no quedarse, no residir\n\nTakaskraskira\n \n(adj,adv)\n \n–\n \nunstoppable, zealous, zealously\n \n/ imparable, celoso\n\nTakaskraskira smalkaia\n \n(\njl16\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto preach/teach zealously, to preach/teach unstoppably\n \n/\npredicar/enseñar celosamente, predicar/enseñar imparablemente\n\nTakaspara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndo not stop, do not impede, do not hinder, do not delay, do not conclude, do not stay, do\nnot remain, do not take a position, do not dwell, do not abide, do not reside, do not live\n \n/ no te detengas, no\nobstaculices, no retrases, no concluyas, no te quedes, no tomes posición, no te detengas, no permanezcas, no\nresidas, no vivas\n\nTala\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nblood\n \n/ sangre\n\n(Construct:\n \nTâilia\n;\n \nTâliam, Talyam\n;\n \nTalia, Talya,Tâlia\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlv-216\n):\n \ntala plapi ba klasbi ya ba saîka nani\n \n–\n \nmedicines that thicken blood (that is running; that is thin)\n \n/ medicamentos que\nespesan la sangre (que fluye; que es líquida))",
